## Custom Features (Deviations from Upstream)

### Built-in Rich-Text Compose Editor
- `RichTextEditor(QTextEdit)` with inline image support (paste, drag-and-drop)
- Images stored in temp dir; rewritten to `cid:` references on send
- Formatting shortcuts (Ctrl+B/I/U)
- HTML body with plaintext fallback via `mime_builder`
- External editor still available as escape hatch (`E` key)

### Address Autocomplete
- `AddressCompleter` backed by `notmuch address --output=recipients`
- All addresses preloaded once in a background thread at startup
- Comma-aware token extraction: completes only the active address
- Minimum 2 characters before popup appears (configurable via `compose_autocomplete_min_chars`)

### Per-Account Signatures
- Loaded from `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/dodo/<account>/signature` (plain text)
- Optional `signature.html` for future HTML compose mode
- Swapped automatically when cycling SMTP accounts
- `-- ` prefix per RFC 3676

### Mail Filter Rules
- `settings.filter_rules`: list of `Rule(query, tag_add, tag_remove, move_to, name)`
- Applied automatically after every sync, scoped by `settings.filter_scope_query`
- Manual invocation via `C-r` (`Dodo.apply_filter_rules()`)
- File moves enqueued to the same background worker as delete/archive

### Status Bar
- `MainWindow.show_status(message, kind, duration)` — supported kinds: info/warning/error
- `duration=0` keeps message until replaced (used for sync progress)
- `Dodo.status_message()` convenience method callable from any panel

### Delete Workflow
- `d` moves files to Trash folder (matching Thunderbird/neomutt)
- Strips mbsync UID annotations to avoid duplicate UID errors
- Trash folder auto-detected per account (`[Gmail]/Trash` or `Trash`)
- `d d` (empty trash): adds `T` flag → mbsync expunges on next sync
- `d u` (restore): moves files back to INBOX + tags `-trash +inbox`
- Centralized in `dodo/actions.py`

### Archive-to-Local Workflow
- `A` moves files to local-only Archive Maildir (outside synced IMAP folders)
- Refuses threads without categorizing tags
- Centralized in `dodo/actions.py`

### Sync Progress
- `SyncMailThread.progress` signal emits per-mailbox status during sync
- Status bar shows real-time: "Syncing: gmail... INBOX Finances ..."
- Final summary parsed from mbsync output: "Sync: +3 new, 2 flagged"

### Other Changes
- **Split-pane UX**: persistent thread preview (configurable via `thread_pane_position`)
- **Thread auto-open**: `j`/`k` navigation auto-opens selected thread after 150ms debounce
- **Neomutt-style nav**: `j`/`k`/`s`/`a`/`d`/`A` are global — work from thread preview too
- **Marked-thread bulk actions**: `s` marks threads, then `d`/`a`/`A` operate on all marked in view
- **Bulk file moves**: background `QThread` serialises file I/O; `notmuch new` fires via `batch_done` signal AFTER moves land on disk
- **Persistent search tabs**: open searches saved/restored across sessions
- **`force_dark_mode` setting**: passes `--force-dark-mode` to Chromium (default on)
- **Double-buffered views**: `QStackedLayout(StackAll)` keeps both QWebEngineViews compositing to prevent white flash on page load
- **Fixed flagged icon**: `󰉀` (NerdFont) for consistency with other tag icons
- **Thread count column** (`#`): shows fa-comments icon + count for multi-message threads
- **Plaintext fallback**: HTML mode degrades to plaintext when no HTML part exists
- **Case-insensitive email matching**: `email_is_me` and `email_smtp_account_index`
- **Three-column help window** layout
- **Column order**: `date | # | from | subject | tags`
- **Archive refuses** threads without categorizing tags (not just inbox/unread)
- `deleted`/`killed`/`spam` excluded from searches by default
- **`mail_root` setting**: configurable Maildir root (default `~/Mail`)

### Refactoring History

#### 2025-07-29 — Dashboard Removal & Housekeeping
- **Removed `DashboardPanel`/`DashboardModel`**: unused; simplified codebase by ~480 lines
- **Extracted `compose_threads.py`**: `EditorThread` and `SendmailThread` moved out of `compose.py`
- **Cleaned dead code**: shadow `columns` in `tag.py`, commented-out code in `util.py`
- **Converted `html2html` lambda to `def`** for debuggability
- **Fixed `_shared_addresses`**: initialised as empty list instead of None, avoiding None-check fragility
- **`_BulkMoveWorker` exit**: exits immediately when no more batches are pending rather than waiting for timeout
- **Double-buffer comment**: documented why `QStackedLayout.StackAll` is needed (white-flash prevention)

#### 2025-07-24 — Actions Mixin & Selection Fixes
- **`dodo/actions.py`**: `MarkableActionsMixin` extracts duplicated tag/archive/delete logic from SearchPanel into three hooks (`_marked_query`, `_current_thread_id`, `_current_thread_tags`).
  - `_unique_dest()` prevents filename collisions when UID stripping produces duplicate basenames
  - `_resolve_stale_path()` finds mbsync-renamed files (flag sync changes `:2,` → `:2,S`)
  - `batch_done` signal fires AFTER file moves land on disk
- **`dodo/search.py`**: `_select_near_row()` fallback in `refresh()` when deleted thread ID is gone
- **`dodo/keymap.py`**: configurable tag hotkeys (1-9) via `settings.tag_hotkeys`; hotkeys added to global keymap
- **`dodo/thread.py`**: Date shown in local timezone; Message ID hidden from header
- **`dodo/app.py`**: `Dodo.toggle_tag_hotkey()` for global tag hotkey delegation; two-phase logging setup

## Key Learnings

### mbsync Flag Sync Renames Files
When `synchronize_flags=true`, mbsync renames Maildir files to reflect flag
changes (e.g. `:2,` → `:2,S` when Seen flag syncs).  Notmuch still has the old
path until `notmuch new` runs.  Fix: `_resolve_stale_path()` globs the parent
directory for the same basename stem.

### Filename Collisions After UID Stripping
`_strip_uid_annotation` removes `,U=\d+` from mbsync filenames.  Two files from
the same host with different UIDs produce the same destination basename.
`_unique_dest()` appends `.1`, `.2`, etc. to prevent silent overwrites.

### Logging
- `settings.log_level` (DEBUG/INFO/WARNING) and `settings.log_file` (path or '')
- Minimal stderr logger set up before config.py loads; full reconfiguration after
- `--verbose` overrides level to INFO for that session

### QWebEngineView White Flash
Chromium tears down the render surface when a `QWebEngineView` is hidden. Using
`QStackedLayout.StackAll` keeps both views compositing at all times — the inactive
view is merely covered, not hidden, so swaps are instant. `QStackedWidget` (which
calls `hide()` on the inactive widget) would reintroduce the flash.

## New Settings
| Setting | Default | Purpose |
|---------|---------|---------|
| `tag_hotkeys` | `{}` | Map number keys to tags for quick toggling |
| `tag_order` | `['marked','Urgent','ToDo','Waiting','Reference','inbox','sent']` | Tag display order in columns |
| `log_level` | `'WARNING'` | Python logging level |
| `log_file` | `''` | Optional log file path |
| `filter_rules` | `[]` | List of `Rule` dataclasses for auto-tagging |
| `filter_scope_query` | `'tag:inbox and tag:unread'` | Limits filter_rules scope |
| `archive_dir` | `'~/Mail/Archive'` | Local-only Archive Maildir |
| `compose_editor_font` | `'DejaVu Sans Mono'` | Font for built-in editor |
| `compose_editor_font_size` | `12` | Font size for built-in editor |
| `compose_autocomplete_min_chars` | `2` | Min chars before address popup |
| `use_signature` | `True` | Enable per-account signatures |
| `thread_pane_position` | `'right'` | Thread preview placement |

## Post-New Hook
Located at `~/.config/notmuch/default/hooks/post-new`:
- Maps `[Gmail]/Spam` → `+spam` tag
- Strips `inbox`/`unread` from `+deleted` messages
- Strips `inbox` from `+spam` messages (Gmail mutual exclusivity)

